#AUTO 60
# DRAM walk — pattern-test a 1 MB window of DRAM to catch bad RAM.
#
# Read-only as far as the probe language is concerned (no W lines);
# the actual write/read pattern test runs in C behind CALL memtest,
# against a fixed 1 MB window at the 1 GB mark of DRAM that is well
# clear of the kernel and the page allocator. It writes four
# marching patterns (0, all-ones, 0x55, 0xAA) plus an
# address-in-address pass and verifies every read-back, logging the
# first failing address or "memtest PASS".
#
# Requires a kernel built with the memtest CALL target (probe engine
# 019; added alongside this script). If CALL memtest logs "unknown
# target", reflash a newer kernel.

LOG DRAM pattern test (1 MB @ 0x40000000)
CALL memtest
LOG DRAM walk complete
